Hi there Doc,<br><br>&gt; There are a lot of broken Sensors in the last Releases. Did no one <br>&gt; noticed? Most of the Sensors do not work correctly.<br><br>&gt; I don't know what is damaged exactly, but here's what i see:<br>&gt; Ray Sensor does not stop pulsing on Contact. Even all Pulsemodes are off.<br>&gt; Collision Sensor is blind to IPO Animated Objects.<br><br>&gt;   It seems that no Sensor has negative Pulses anymore. Message Sensor, Keyboard Sensor ... It seems there comes a second positive Pulse instead a negative by leaving them.<br><br>&gt; Can anybody confirm these Bugs?<br><br><br>Can you do this, it would greatly help with finding and fixing the bugs...<br><br>0) Try it in Preview 13<br><br>1) Create a very simple .blend file that shows the bug when P is pressed, and that also describes ( create a text window ) what should be happening.<br><br>2) Try older versions of Blender ( especially 2.42a ) and let me know if the bug exists also in that version.<br><br>If you can make it easy to find them with a .blend, I'll try to fix em!<br><br>Best regards...<br>Mal<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=27">mal</a> — Wed Jan 10, 2007 8:23 pm</p><hr />
